@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "koroneiki.provisioning.account.search"

Feature:  Koroneiki to Provisioning Account Search
	Testing to assure that koroneiki account search works properly.

Setup:
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | sea.koroneiki1                       |
	| Email Address | sea.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | SEA                                  |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki1                           |
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | sea.koroneiki2                       |
	| Email Address | sea.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | SEA                                  |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki2                           |

Teardown:
	* I wait for "5" seconds
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Korsea - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the first default user ID variable
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Onesea - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the second default user ID variable
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Seakor - ${staticCompanyName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the third default user ID variable
	* I tear down the teams on koroneiki with the following names
	| Korsearch Partner |
	* I tear down the external links for the account "Korsea - ${staticProjectName}" on koroneiki with the following entity id and domain values
	| ${staticDossieraAccountKey}   | salesforce |
	| ${staticDossieraProjectKey}   | dossiera   |
	| ${staticSalesforceProjectKey} | salesforce |
	* I tear down the external links for the account "Seakor - ${staticCompanyName}" on koroneiki with the following entity id and domain values
	| ${staticDossieraAccountKey} | salesforce |
	| ${staticDossieraAccountKey} | dossiera   |
	* I tear down the product purchases on koroneiki made by the account "Korsea - ${staticProjectName}" for the following products
	| DXP Production        |
	| Platinum Subscription |
	| Gold Subscription     |
	| Limited Subscription  |
	* I tear down the product purchases on koroneiki made by the account "Onesea - ${staticProjectName}" for the following products
	| DXP Production        |
	| Platinum Subscription |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from web.liferay.com
	| sea.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| sea.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from customer.liferay.com
	| sea.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| sea.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from koroneiki
	| sea.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| sea.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
 	* I tear down the contacts on koroneiki with the following email addresses
	| sea.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| sea.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Korsea - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Onesea - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Seakor - ${staticCompanyName} |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following "Code" values
	| SEAKORKORSEA |
	| ONESEAONESEA |
	| SEAKOR       |
	* I teardown the tickets with the following keywords from zendesk.liferay.com
	| New Subscription(s) for Korsea - ${staticProjectName} |
	| New Subscription(s) for Seakor - ${staticCompanyName} |
	* I wait for "5" seconds
	* I log out and log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test"
	* I tear down the projects with the following project codes via groovy
	| SEAKORKORSEA |
	| ONESEAONESEA |
	| SEAKOR       |
	* I obtain the IDs of the following user email addresses from zendesk.liferay.com
	| sea.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| sea.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I teardown users with the following userIds "${staticUserIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I obtain the external IDs of the following organizations from zendesk.liferay.com
	| Korsea - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Onesea - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Seakor - ${staticCompanyName} |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds "${staticOrganizationExternalIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId1}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId2}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId3}" from zendesk.liferay.com

Scenario: View T4 project via Search Accounts
	Testing the ability to create a T4 project in Dossiera and viewing the project in the provisioning page via Search Accounts field

	Given I generate several static variables for Provisioning
	And I generate a provisioning company name
	And I generate a provisioning project name
	And I publish a project with no partner RabbitMQ message with routing key "dossiera.provisioning.create" with the following values
	| Account Name                           | Seakor - ${staticCompanyName}              |
	| Address City                           | Diamond Bar                                |
	| Address Country                        | United States                              |
	| Address Postal Code                    | 91765                                      |
	| Address Region                         | California                                 |
	| Address Street                         | 456 Fake Street                            |
	| Contact Email Address                  | sea.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Contact First Name                     | SEA                                        |
	| Contact Last Name                      | Koroneiki1                                 |
	| Dossiera Account Key                   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey}                |
	| Dossiera Address Key 1                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey1}               |
	| Dossiera Address Key 2                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey2}               |
	| Dossiera Contact Key                   | ${staticDossieraContactKey}                |
	| Dossiera Project Key                   | ${staticDossieraProjectKey}                |
	| End Day                                | ${staticEndDay}                            |
	| End Month                              | ${staticEndMonth}                          |
	| End Year                               | ${staticEndYear}                           |
	| Industry                               | Automotive                                 |
	| Owner Email Address                    | sea.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Owner First Name                       | SEA                                        |
	| Owner Last Name                        | Koroneiki2                                 |
	| Partner First Line Support             | false                                      |
	| Product Type                           | New                                        |
	| Product Name                           | DXP Production                             |
	| Project Name                           | Korsea - ${staticProjectName}              |
	| Renewal                                | false                                      |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Key             | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityKey}          |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 1 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey1} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 2 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey2} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Sold By         | Liferay US                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Stage Name      | Closed Won                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Territory       | United States                              |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Type            | New Business                               |
	| Salesforce Owner User Key              | ${staticSalesforceOwnerUserKey}            |
	| Salesforce Project Key                 | ${staticSalesforceProjectKey}              |
	| Start Day                              | ${staticStartDay}                          |
	| Start Month                            | ${staticStartMonth}                        |
	| Start Year                             | ${staticStartYear}                         |
	| Subscription Level                     | Platinum                                   |
	| Version Number                         | 7.1                                        |
	And I create a team with the name "Korsearch Partner" for the account "Korsea - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I assign the team with the name "Korsearch Partner" on the account "Korsea - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Partner |
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "test@liferay.com" with password "kwSgiajslgb7ecsD"
	And I type in the keyword "Korsea" via send keys into the Search Accounts field
	And I click on search accounts button
	Then I should be able to view an account on the provisioning index with the name "Korsea - ${staticProjectName}" and the following values
	| Name    | Korsea - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Code    | SEAKORKORSEA                  |
	| Partner | Korsearch Partner             |
	| Region  | United States                 |
	| SLA     | Platinum                      |
	| Tier    | T4                            |
	| State   | ACTIVE                        |

